1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,620
Right now, somewhere in the world, a neural

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:05,700
network is learning. It has billions of tiny

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,210
dials, and every single dial must be nudged

4
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:10,800
in exactly the right direction, by exactly the

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,120
right amount. But how does it know which

6
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,760
way to turn one dial, buried deep inside,

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,670
many layers away from the answer it is

8
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:20,090
judged on? The answer is one idea from

9
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:22,980
calculus, an idea you may have memorized, without

10
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,920
ever feeling why it works. The chain rule,

11
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,660
it is the same idea that tells you

12
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:29,920
how fast a shadow races across the ground,

13
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:32,120
when a lamp swings overhead, and how a

14
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,730
tiny change in an interest rate ripples through

15
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:37,050
a bank balance. In the next seven minutes,

16
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:39,210
we will build the chain rule from nothing.

17
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:41,690
We start with a simple picture, three gears

18
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:44,560
turning one another. Then we derive the rule

19
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:47,730
from first principles, using only the definition of

20
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:49,770
a derivative. We test it on a real

21
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:52,370
example, the sign of X squared, and watch

22
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:55,150
the numbers agree. And finally, we return to

23
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:58,080
that neural network, and discover that its entire

24
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,000
learning process is this one rule, repeated again

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,350
and again. The year album day. By the

26
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:06,120
end, you will not just know the formula,

27
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,470
you will see it. Imagine three gears in

28
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:11,170
a row, glowing against a dark background. The

29
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:14,070
first gear, call it gear A, meshes with

30
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:17,110
the second, gear B. Gear B, meshes with

31
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,940
the third, gear C. Suppose every time gear

32
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,260
A makes one full turn, gear B makes

33
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,850
two full turns. So gear B moves twice

34
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:27,510
as fast as gear A. Label that rate

35
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:30,690
on screen, times two. Now suppose every time

36
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:32,530
gear B makes one full turn, gear C

37
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:35,080
makes three full turns. So gear C moves

38
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:37,520
three times as fast as gear B. Label

39
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:40,670
that rate times three. Here is the question.

40
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:43,140
When gear A turns once, how many times

41
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,870
does gear C turn? Gear A turns once,

42
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:48,750
gear B turns twice. And each of those

43
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:51,440
two turns sends gear C around three times,

44
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:54,310
two times three, six full turns. Watch the

45
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:56,960
two and the three slide together and merge

46
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,500
into a six, rates multiply. Hold on to

47
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,130
that, because that is the chain rule in

48
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:04,420
disguise. A derivative is just a rate, how

49
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:07,030
fast an output changes compared to its input.

50
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:09,360
And when one thing drives a second thing,

51
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,990
which drives a third, the rates multiply. Now

52
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:14,650
let us swap the gears for functions. Picture

53
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:17,540
two machines sitting side by side, connected by

54
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:20,320
a pipe. A number X enters the first

55
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:23,360
machine, which we call G. Outcomes a new

56
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:26,630
number U. Then U enters the second machine

57
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:30,440
called F. And out comes the final number

58
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,720
Y. So Y equals F of G of

59
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:35,271
X, a function inside a function. We want

60
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:37,400
to know if we nudge X by a

61
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:40,630
tiny amount, how much does Y move? Watch

62
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:43,330
the nudge travel. On the number line, we

63
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,550
push X forward by a tiny step, which

64
00:02:45,550 --> 00:02:48,450
we call Delta X. The first machine stretches

65
00:02:48,450 --> 00:02:50,460
or squeezes that step into a new step

66
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,640
in U called Delta U. Then the second

67
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,750
machine stretches or squeezes Delta U into a

68
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:58,310
step in Y called Delta Y. Each machine

69
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:00,720
behaves like a gear with its own local

70
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:04,120
rate. The first machine's rate compares Delta U

71
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,880
to Delta X. The second machine's rate compares

72
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,150
Delta Y to Delta U. The nudge travels

73
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:12,160
down the chain, getting scaled at every link,

74
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,940
let us make this precise. The derivative of

75
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,830
Y with respect to X is defined as

76
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:19,060
a limit. The change in Y divided by

77
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,890
the change in X as the change in

78
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:23,840
X shrinks towards zero. Now comes one small

79
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,350
trick. We rewrite Delta Y over Delta X

80
00:03:26,350 --> 00:03:30,150
as two fractions multiplied together. Delta Y over

81
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:32,770
Delta U times Delta U over Delta X

82
00:03:32,770 --> 00:03:36,280
is that allowed. Watch the screen. Delta U

83
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:38,580
sits on the top of one fraction and

84
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,580
the bottom of the other, so it cancels,

85
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:43,450
leaving exactly what we started with. Nothing has

86
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:45,680
changed. We have only added a stepping stone

87
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:48,080
in the middle. Now look at each piece.

88
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,550
The right fraction Delta U over Delta X

89
00:03:50,550 --> 00:03:53,080
is the rate of the first machine. The

90
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,250
left fraction Delta Y over Delta U is

91
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:58,170
the rate of the second machine. Next, let

92
00:03:58,170 --> 00:04:01,300
Delta X shrink towards zero, because the first

93
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:04,170
machine is smooth. When Delta X shrinks, Delta

94
00:04:04,170 --> 00:04:06,470
U shrinks right along with it. So both

95
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:09,760
fractions settle into true derivatives. The left fraction

96
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:12,380
becomes the derivative of Y with respect to

97
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,310
U. The right fraction becomes the derivative of

98
00:04:15,310 --> 00:04:17,750
U with respect to X. And there it

99
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:20,430
is. The derivative of Y with respect to

100
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:23,190
X equals the derivative of Y with respect

101
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:25,300
to U times the derivative of U with

102
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,870
respect to X. In plain words, the rate

103
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:30,160
of the outer machine measured at the inner

104
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:32,630
machine's output times the rate of the inner

105
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:35,610
machine. One honest footnote, if Delta U ever

106
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:39,040
lands on exactly zero, the canceling step breaks

107
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,320
and a fully rigorous proof handles that case

108
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,620
separately. But the heart of the idea is

109
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:46,310
complete. The total rate is the product of

110
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:48,780
the rates along the chain. Let us test

111
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,380
it on Y equals the sign of X

112
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:53,370
squared. On the left, a parabola, on the

113
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:56,580
right, a sine wave. The inner machine is

114
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:59,050
U equals X squared. The outer machine is

115
00:04:59,050 --> 00:05:01,430
Y equals the sign of U. The inner

116
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:03,990
rate is 2X. The outer rate is the

117
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:07,210
cosine of U. Multiply them, put X squared

118
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:09,140
back in for U. And we get the

119
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:12,550
derivative equals 2X times the cosine of X

120
00:05:12,550 --> 00:05:15,640
squared. But is the formula telling the truth?

121
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,651
Let us check at X equals 1, at

122
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,840
X equals 1, the inner rate is 2.

123
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:22,700
So the first machine stretches every tiny nudge

124
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:24,960
by a factor of 2. The outer rate

125
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,330
is the cosine of 1, which is about

126
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:33,000
0.54. Multiply 2 times 0.54, about 1.08. Now

127
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,320
the brute force check with no formula at

128
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:38,240
all. Nudge X from 1 to 1.001. Watch

129
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:44,700
X squared move from 1 to 1.002001, about

130
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:47,040
twice the nudge. Then the sign of that

131
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:51,990
moves from about 0.8415 to about 0.8426, a

132
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:56,640
change of roughly 0.00108. Divide that change by

133
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:59,800
our nudge of 0.001 and we get about

134
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:02,970
1.08, the formula and the brute force agree.

135
00:06:02,970 --> 00:06:05,450
A common mistake is to write only the

136
00:06:05,450 --> 00:06:08,400
cosine of X squared, forgetting the inner rate.

137
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:11,090
That means forgetting the first gear. Now, back

138
00:06:11,090 --> 00:06:13,680
to our neural network. Picture three layers of

139
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:16,920
glowing nodes joined by thousands of thin lines.

140
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:19,360
One weight sits deep inside. On a single

141
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,840
line, it shapes a neuron's input that passes

142
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,600
through an activation function to become the neuron's

143
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:27,560
output. That output feeds the next layer, which

144
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,470
finally produces a prediction. The prediction is compared

145
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:32,760
to the truth, giving one number called the

146
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:35,360
loss, which measures how wrong the network is.

147
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,530
That is a long chain of functions, each

148
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:40,050
one inside the next, asking how the loss

149
00:06:40,050 --> 00:06:41,890
changes when we nudge that one weight is

150
00:06:41,890 --> 00:06:43,900
a chain rule problem, with a rate at

151
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:47,510
every link. Back propagation simply walks backward from

152
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:49,840
the loss, multiplying one local rate at a

153
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,600
time, like gears turning in reverse. When it

154
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,820
arrives at the weight, the product tells it

155
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:56,840
exactly which way to turn and by how

156
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:58,900
much. Then it does the same for every

157
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:01,570
other weight, billions of times. There is no

158
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:04,520
new mathematics hiding inside. It is the chain

159
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:07,010
rule applied at enormous scale, so the next

160
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:09,110
time you meet the derivative of Y with

161
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,960
respect to X equals the derivative of Y

162
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,930
with respect to U times the derivative of

163
00:07:13,930 --> 00:07:16,060
U with respect to X, do not see

164
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:19,400
symbols, see gears. The nudge enters at one

165
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:22,020
end, get stretched or squeezed by every link

166
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,960
along the way, and what comes out is

167
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:26,340
the product of all those stretches that is

168
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,440
why a shadow, a bank balance, and a

169
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,440
billion-dial neural network can all be understood by

170
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:33,640
the same idea. In the next video, we

171
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,080
will watch back propagation run on a real

172
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:40,920
network, one step at time. See you there.

